    "malloc_history reports a dynamically-enabled logging warning with 816 pre-existing unstacked blocks for storage and 805 blocks plus 9 VM regions for view; totals exclude unstacked allocations.",
    "Process heap/RSS/high-water are separate from logged live allocation heap and VM, and do not identify retained objects.",
    "Graphs and full call trees are local artifacts in /tmp/merenda-utf8-profile; graph files include full stack history and are not checked into the repository.",
    "Per-sample targetStages includes measurements after the graph checkpoint (such as resized); these later stages are not represented in the captured graph.",
    "Instruments Allocations launch failed to attach on this machine; dtrace required root access. Memory graphs were captured with same-user Apple leaks and MallocStackLogging instead."
